# Long Road Architecture

Oregon Trail–style trail simulation. Code lives in assembly-defined layers under `Assets/_Game/` and `Assets/Packages/`.

## Layers

- **LongRoad.Domain** — any logic that does **not** need Unity (`noEngineReferences`). Pure C# rules, interfaces, formulas.
- **LongRoad.Core** — **base** systems and shared implementations (including shared **game** systems) that use Unity or are reused across features. References Domain + Packages.
- **LongRoad** — main game pipeline, UI, scene managers, feature systems that compose Core/Domain.
- **LongRoad.Packages** — local/third-party code; never depends on game assemblies.

## Dependency rule

`Domain` is isolated (no Unity / no Packages). `Core` and `LongRoad` may use Domain and Packages. Packages never depends on game code.

## Placement heuristic

| Put here | When | Examples |
|----------|------|----------|
| Domain | No Unity types needed | Pure rationing math, win/lose checks, interfaces (`IInit`), RNG resolution without SO |
| Core | Shared base / reusable game system (may use Unity) | `LongRoadScriptable`, `Person` / `PersonEntity`, `GameEventBase`, `LocalizationManager`, behaviour bases |
| LongRoad | Feature or pipeline that uses those bases | `GameManager`, `LocalManager`, `GameUIManager`, `GamePipeline`, services, UI panels, concrete events |
| Packages | Vendored utilities | NaughtyAttributes, DOTween |
| `_Game/Resources` | Game assets | Characters, traits, locale tables, scenes |

Do not treat Core as “Unity glue only” or as “everything game-related.” Prefer Domain when logic is pure; Core when it is a shared base; LongRoad when it is feature/orchestration/UI.

## Naming — Manager vs Service

- **`*Manager`**: `MonoBehaviour` controllers that own scene/global wiring (prefer `LongRoadBehaviour` / `LongRoadBehaviourCore`).
- **`*Service`**: plain non-MonoBehaviour orchestration; implement `IService` (`LongRoad.Domain.Interfaces`); place under `Services/` (`LongRoad.Services`). Pass dependencies through the **constructor** (avoid service `Init` for wiring).
- **Exception**: `GamePipeline` — full game turn loop; no `Service` suffix; lives at `LongRoad` assembly root (not under `Services/`).
